<NPR><ITA>TEMPLATE INSTRUCTION:  THIS AND OTHER TEMPLATE INSTRUCTIONS PERTAIN TO THE USE 
OF THIS TEMPLATE.  DO NOT INCLUDE THESE IN A SPECIFICATION.  Deselect the Template_Instr 
tailoring option tag before releasing the Master or publishing the Job.</ITA></NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR><ITA>This template is for use as an aid in the development of a new UFGS master section 
and reflects paragraph titles and sequence detailed in the <URL HREF="https://www.wbdg.org/dod/ufc/ufc-1-300-02">UFS 1-300-02</URL> Unified 
Facilities Guide Specifications (UFGS) Format Standard.</ITA></NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR><ITA>It is important that UFGS authors understand that the paragraphs listed below 
are not mandatory.  Use only those paragraphs that are applicable to the specified 
subject, and add any applicable requirements not listed.  It is important to 
follow the sequence of information provided herein even when adjusting the paragraph 
titles to fit the specified subject matter.  This template does not contain 
all of the paragraphs listed in the CSI SectionFormat.  Refer to CSI SectionFormat 
for further guidance on paragraph structure.</ITA></NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR><ITA>Highlighted (HLS) text within the section banner indicates variables.  Remove 
highlighting by deleting the tags.</ITA></NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR><ITA>There are three standard notes used in UFGS:  1.  The GENERAL Note following 
this note; 2.  The note following the title of the REFERENCES paragraph;  and 
3.  The note following the title of the SUBMITTALS paragraph.  When notes to 
the designer are necessary, they are placed between the title and the text.</ITA></NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR><ITA>There are two standard text paragraphs used in UFGS:  1.  The text in the REFERENCES 
paragraph preceeding the listing of references; and 2.  The text in the SUBMITTALS 
paragraph preceeding the listing of submittals required.</ITA></NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR><ITA>Text in paragraphs other than the standard notes and standard text are for information 
for the template user.</ITA></NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR><ITA>In guide specifications, provide units of measure in both Metric and English 
Systems.  Using SpecsIntact tagging, enter the Metric measurement followed by 
the English measurement.  Example, "For sizes<MET> 40 mm</MET><ENG> 1-1/2 inches</ENG> and smaller..."</ITA></NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR><ITA>Paragraph and subparagraph numbering to the sixth level must have titles and 
be completely numeric.  Below the paragraph or subparagraph level, titles are 
optional and list and item tags may be used with alternating alpha-numeric designation.  
This format will not translate to the Alphanumeric format and will not automatically 
renumber.  Manual numbering is required.</ITA></NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR><ITA>Refer to the SpecsIntact Help for instructions on how to tag paragraphs using 
the SpecsIntact software.  In order to maintain the proper tagging structure, 
it is suggested that this template be used with the tags turned on, then replace 
the template text with text of the new section.</ITA></NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
</TAI><NTE><BRK/>
<AST/> <BRK/>
<NPR>Adhere to <URL HREF="https://www.wbdg.org/dod/ufc/ufc-1-300-02">UFS 1-300-02</URL> Specifications (UFGS) Format Standard when editing this guide specification 
